NAME
       watch - run a command again and again and show its output full screen

SYNOPSIS
       watch [-n SECONDS] [-d] COMMAND

DESCRIPTION
       watch runs COMMAND every 2 seconds and shows its latest output on a
       cleared screen, with a header showing the interval, the command, the
       host name and the time. Use it to see something change while you work
       in another terminal, such as a service starting or a file growing.
       Press Ctrl+C to stop. Quote COMMAND when it contains a pipe.

OPTIONS
       -n, --interval=SECONDS
              Run the command every SECONDS seconds.

       -d, --differences
              Highlight what changed since the last run.

EXAMPLES
           watch -n 1 'ls -l /var/log/messages'
           watch 'systemctl is-active httpd'

SEE ALSO
       top(1), tail(1), sleep(1)
